=== p2-windows · W7 · page:dashboard/Dashboard (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:dashboard/Dashboard   kind=page   web route=/
Web source  : web/src/features/dashboard/pages/DashboardPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection +
  registration + diagnostics + data ports, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed),
  <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly
  as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage / EnergyPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "DashboardPage.xaml + DashboardPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Dashboard" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("Dashboard", already in
  RouteTable.cs L91 → path "" / index route /) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004, P1/S8): the manifest's two data sources are bound to the generated OpenAPI contract client
  through observable ViewModel ports.
    * useAuthStatus → GET /auth/status : IAuthStatusSource → AuthStatusClientSource (DashboardPage.Source.cs) reads
      generated operation get_api_v1_auth_status cache-then-network through the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine, caching
      raw JSON so the snake_case wire shape round-trips, and parses {authenticated:bool} into DashboardAuthStatus.
    * useSyncVehicles → POST /vehicles/sync : IVehicleSyncGateway → VehicleSyncClientGateway posts generated
      operation post_api_v1_vehicles_sync through the contract client; failures map through ApiErrorMapper. Both
      operation ids resolve against the generated ApiEndpoints table (Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs L177 + L513). No
      HTTP touches the view. The parameterless page uses headless-safe defaults (EmptyAuthStatusSource yields a
      resolved "not connected" snapshot; NoopVehicleSyncGateway is a benign success) so the surface is fully
      renderable in tests / design-time hosts.
- The web page composes a header (PageContainer title/subtitle + a header-actions toolbar), a stack of conditional
  banners (ThemeFirstRunBanner, customize hint, anyError, auth-not-connected), and a body that switches on
  vehiclesLoading / vehicles / EmptyOnboarding. The manifest narrows THIS unit to the page chrome + the two
  EmptyOnboarding GlassPanels (DashboardPage.tsx L691 outer hero + L724 feature card ×4); the widget grid is the
  union of ~95 separate dashboard-widget parity units and is out of this unit's scope. The native port reproduces
  every in-scope region as a visible Fluent region per ADR-006:
    * header  : PageTitle + Subhead + TsDataFreshness chip; the customize/normal toolbars (TsButton row).
    * banners : TsAlertBanner(Info) theme first-run (title/body + Open/Maybe-later actions, dismissible);
                TsAlertBanner(Info) customize hint (message + Add-widgets action, normal-mode, dismissible);
                TsAlertBanner(Danger) failure banner (web anyError); TsAlertBanner(Warning) account-not-connected
                (notConnected title + connectPrompt/settings/toStart message + Settings action → NavigateTo settings).
    * edit    : the edit-mode hint TsGlassPanel (web editHint), the reset-confirmation TsAlertBanner (web
                layout.resetMessage, shown on Reset, confirm → CommandRequested(Reset)), and the New-Dashboard
                TsButton surface (web dashboard.newDashboard, shown on Templates).
    * body    : the three declared data states — loading → TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; error →
                TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry → RefreshAsync; success → the onboarding hero (GlassPanel1)
                whose footer is the four feature cards (GlassPanel2). Never a blank region.
- The onboarding hero branches on auth.authenticated exactly as web EmptyOnboarding: authenticated → "Sync Your
  Vehicles" / syncDesc / "Sync Vehicles" (→ ViewModel.SyncAsync, web syncVehicles.mutate()); unauthenticated →
  "Welcome to TeslaSync" / desc / "Connect Tesla Account" (→ NavigateTo settings). The projection resolves BOTH
  branches of every onboarding ternary unconditionally so a single Project() references all 36 manifest keys
  regardless of the model branch (asserted headlessly via RecordingLocalizer).
- Toolbar: Customize/Done toggle the real local edit-mode (web editMode) on the ViewModel; Refresh → RefreshAsync;
  Reset opens the confirmation banner; Templates reveals the New-Dashboard surface. The remaining chrome commands
  (Undo/Redo/AddWidget/AutoArrange/Templates/Kiosk/PrintSnapshot/NewDashboard/Reset) raise the documented
  CommandRequested event seam for the host to handle (the widget/layout/kiosk/print subsystems are separate parity
  units) — the established repo pattern (NavigationRequested/BackRequested/CloseRequested on sibling pages), not a
  stub.
- Live SSE / staleness (ADR-013): neither declared data source is a live signal stream (auth-status is a one-shot
  read; sync is a command), so no SSE subscription or >2-min staleness indicator is required for this unit; the
  header freshness chip still reflects the last auth read (UpdatedAt/IsFetching/IsError).
- SI units (P1/S5): this surface renders zero unit-bearing physical fields (no distances, speeds, temps, energy,
  pressure) — only auth state, onboarding copy and command labels — so the SI converter boundary is trivially
  honored (nothing to convert).
- i18n (ADR-014): all 36 manifest keys already exist in Strings/en/Resources.resw as translation.* entries (generated
  from the shared web i18n source); the surface resolves every label through the ILocalizer facade with the web key
  names (bare, matching the sibling pages' GetString convention) and the verbatim English defaults, so no literal is
  hardcoded. The ar/he catalogs fall back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties.Name on the page (document title), the onboarding hero and each feature card;
  TsButton labels seed their own Narrator names; the icon-only Refresh button gets an explicit localized name; the
  banners are live regions (TsBannerBase). Light/dark + high-contrast honored via the W2 design tokens (TsGlassPanel
  Mica/glass surface + token brushes); no hardcoded colors.
- Headless test wiring: the Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel files were added as <Compile Include> links to
  TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view DashboardPage.cs is excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). The card
  accent is a Core-only DashboardCardAccent enum in the Model (mapped to the component GlassGlow only in the view) so
  the headless files carry zero UI dependency.
- Build-time defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) the headless Model.cs
  initially referenced the component GlassGlow enum, which is unavailable to the Core-only test project that links it
  — replaced with the Core-only DashboardCardAccent enum, mapped to GlassGlow in the view; (2) the new .cs files were
  authored with CRLF line endings, which dotnet format flagged as ENDOFLINE — normalized to LF (UTF-8, no BOM) to
  match the repo. Both fully repaired; app + solution build 0 errors / 0 warnings and format-verify is clean.

